title: PostTutorial_WhatsNext
tags: companion guidance progression
---
// Triggers after tutorial complete + first quiet moment (no wave active, player idle 30s)
<<if $tutorialComplete == true and $postTutorialGuidanceGiven == false>>

{$companionName}: You've got the basics down. Four towers, a companion, and {$petName} at your side.

{$companionName}: But this is just the beginning. Elarion needs more than watchtowers to survive.

-> What should I focus on?
    <<jump PostTutorial_PathOverview>>
-> I'll figure it out.
    {$companionName}: Fair enough. But if you need direction, talk to me anytime.
    <<set $postTutorialGuidanceGiven to true>>

<<endif>>
===

title: PostTutorial_PathOverview
tags: companion guidance
---
{$companionName}: You've got options. Depends on what kind of defender you want to be.

-> Tell me about defending the village.
    <<jump Path_Defense>>
-> What about exploring outside?
    <<jump Path_Exploration>>
-> How do I get stronger?
    <<jump Path_Grinding>>
-> What's out there to discover?
    <<jump Path_Discovery>>

===

title: Path_Defense
tags: companion guidance defense
---
{$companionName}: The walls hold, but they won't hold forever. Not against what's coming.

{$companionName}: Here's what you can do right now:

{$companionName}: Upgrade your towers. The Blacksmith at the Forge can reinforce them — wood becomes stone, stone becomes iron. Each tier hits harder and takes more punishment.

{$companionName}: Place new towers at chokepoints. Not just at the gates — think about where enemies cluster. A Flame Tower in a narrow path burns everything that walks through.

{$companionName}: And the walls themselves. Walk up to the ramparts. You can place Ballistae and Boiling Oil Cauldrons up there — nothing like raining fire from above.

-> What about the Heartwood?
    {$companionName}: The Heartwood responds to survival. The longer you defend it, the more power it grants.
    {$companionName}: After five waves, you'll feel it — Root Spikes, a new ability. The ground itself fights for you.
    {$companionName}: Survive ten? The Heartwood's healing aura covers the whole village.
    {$companionName}: Twenty waves... well. Let's get there first.
-> Can {$petName} help defend?
    {$companionName}: Absolutely. Set {$petName} to Defend mode at the Pet House. They'll patrol near your towers and attack anything that gets close.
    {$companionName}: But that means {$petName} isn't gathering resources. Trade-off.
    {$companionName}: Later, when you tame more Echoes, you can split them — some defend, some gather. Build a proper war pack.

{$companionName}: Defense is the heart of what we do. Everything else supports it.

-> What else can I do?
    <<jump PostTutorial_PathOverview>>
-> Got it. I'll fortify.
    <<set $postTutorialGuidanceGiven to true>>
===

title: Path_Exploration
tags: companion guidance exploration
---
{$companionName}: Beyond the gates, the world opens up. And it's not friendly.

{$companionName}: Head through any gate and you'll find the Marches — the lands around Elarion. Rich in resources, crawling with enemies.

{$companionName}: You'll find resource nodes out there. Wood groves, iron veins, crystal deposits. Each one can be claimed.

-> Claimed?
    {$companionName}: Clear the enemies around a node, and it's yours. Build an outpost on it — a small forward base.
    {$companionName}: Your Echoes can harvest from claimed nodes. {$petName} brings resources back automatically if you assign them.
    {$companionName}: But claimed nodes attract attention. The enemy wants those resources too. You'll need to defend what you take.
    {$companionName}: The richer the node, the harder they'll hit. Silver veins and crystal deposits? Expect war parties.
-> How far can I go?
    {$companionName}: As far as your courage takes you. But it gets dangerous fast.
    {$companionName}: The Inner Marches are close — a minute's walk. Goblins, mostly. Good for early resources.
    {$companionName}: The Border Marches are further. Orc warbands. Tougher, but iron and rare herbs grow there.
    {$companionName}: The Deep Wilds... that's where the Elementals roam. Fire, ice, storm — fragments of the World Ash gone feral. Don't go alone.
    {$companionName}: And beyond that? The Ancient Frontiers. Dragon territory. Nobody's come back from there. Yet.
-> What about getting back to the village?
    {$companionName}: Every outpost you build has a Return Portal. Step through and you're back at the Heartwood instantly.
    {$companionName}: But getting OUT there takes time. The further you go, the longer the walk. Plan your trips.
    {$companionName}: Later, you might be able to send caravans — supply runs that carry resources back while you keep exploring. But those can be ambushed.

{$companionName}: Exploration is how Elarion grows. Every node you claim, every outpost you build — the village gets stronger.

-> What else can I do?
    <<jump PostTutorial_PathOverview>>
-> Time to explore.
    <<set $postTutorialGuidanceGiven to true>>
===

title: Path_Grinding
tags: companion guidance combat leveling
---
{$companionName}: You want to get stronger? Good. You'll need to.

{$companionName}: There are a few ways to gain experience and power:

{$companionName}: Fight waves. Every enemy you kill earns XP. Clear a wave, earn a bonus. The harder the wave, the bigger the reward.

{$companionName}: Explore and fight in the overworld. The camps out in the Marches are full of Orcs and Goblins — tougher than wave enemies, but the XP is worth it.

-> What happens when I level up?
    {$companionName}: The Heartwood responds. You'll feel a surge — new power flowing through you.
    {$companionName}: Every few levels, you unlock a new ability or a talent. The Arcane Tower can help you focus those.
    {$companionName}: And your companion — me — I get stronger too. We're connected to the same root.
-> Can I upgrade my gear?
    {$companionName}: The Blacksmith. Talk to him at the Forge. He can reinforce your weapon, strengthen your armor.
    {$companionName}: But he needs materials. Iron from the mines, wood from the groves, crystals from the deep nodes.
    {$companionName}: Everything loops back to gathering. Fight to level up, gather to upgrade, upgrade to fight harder things.
-> What about {$petName}?
    {$companionName}: Echoes grow with you. The more {$petName} harvests or fights, the stronger they become.
    {$companionName}: And you can tame more. Craft better offerings at the crafting stations — Campfire first, then the Herbal Mortar and Brewing Kettle as your outposts grow.
    {$companionName}: Rarer Echoes hide in deeper zones. A Stonebear in the mountains. A Starveil Stag beyond the ancient groves. Worth the trip.

{$companionName}: Power isn't given in Elarion. It's earned. Every level, every upgrade, every Echo tamed.

-> What else can I do?
    <<jump PostTutorial_PathOverview>>
-> Let's get grinding.
    <<set $postTutorialGuidanceGiven to true>>
===

title: Path_Discovery
tags: companion guidance dungeons secrets
---
{$companionName}: There are things out there that most people don't know about. Old things.

{$companionName}: The world is full of secrets left behind when the World Ash fell.

-> Like what?
    {$companionName}: Dungeons. Hidden beneath the surface — old temples, collapsed tunnels, forgotten vaults.
    {$companionName}: The monks of the Verdant Watch sealed some of them centuries ago. The seals are weakening.
    {$companionName}: Find a dungeon entrance in the overworld and you can explore it. Traps, puzzles, enemies — and at the end, something worth the risk.
    {$companionName}: Rare crafting materials. Ancient weapons. Lore fragments that reveal the true history of the World Ash.
-> Can I build my own bases out there?
    {$companionName}: Outposts, yes. At claimed resource nodes.
    {$companionName}: Start with a simple Resource Outpost — a harvesting camp. Then upgrade it. Add a Watchtower for defense. A Forward Camp for resting.
    {$companionName}: The further you build from Elarion, the more dangerous it gets — but the rewards scale with the risk.
    {$companionName}: Eventually you'll have a network. Elarion at the center, outposts radiating outward. A kingdom, not just a village.
-> What about the Echoes out there?
    {$companionName}: The rarest Echoes don't come to you. You have to find them.
    {$companionName}: Deep in the wilds, after clearing camps or during special events — "Wandering Spirit" moments. An Echo appears, watching.
    {$companionName}: Craft the right offering. Approach with respect. And if you're strong enough... they'll bond with you.
    {$companionName}: A Windrider Hawk scouts ahead and reveals hidden nodes. A Stonebear can tank hits that would kill you. Each one changes how you play.
-> Are there dragons?
    {$companionName}: ...yes. But not like the stories say.
    {$companionName}: Dragons are the oldest living things. Born from the World Ash before the Sundering. Four bloodlines:
    {$companionName}: Cinderwyrms in the volcanic west. Frostfangs in the frozen peaks. Thorndrakes in the deep forest. Stonebacks in the mountains.
    {$companionName}: They don't serve anyone. But they watch. And if Elarion grows strong enough — if you prove you're worth it — one might perch on your walls.
    {$companionName}: That's endgame. Very endgame. But it's out there.

{$companionName}: This world is bigger than it looks from inside the walls. Go find out how big.

-> What else can I do?
    <<jump PostTutorial_PathOverview>>
-> I'm going exploring.
    <<set $postTutorialGuidanceGiven to true>>
===

title: Companion_Reminder_Defend
tags: companion ambient contextual
---
// Triggers when player hasn't started a wave in 10+ minutes
{$companionName}: It's been quiet. Too quiet. Might want to start a wave before they choose when to attack instead.
===

title: Companion_Reminder_Explore
tags: companion ambient contextual
---
// Triggers when player has 4 towers but hasn't left the village
{$companionName}: The village is secure for now. There's a whole world past those gates. Resources, camps, maybe even an Echo waiting for you.
===

title: Companion_Reminder_Upgrade
tags: companion ambient contextual
---
// Triggers when player has enough resources to upgrade a tower but hasn't
<<if $wood >= 100 and $stone >= 50>>
{$companionName}: You've got enough materials to upgrade a tower. The Blacksmith can help — stronger towers mean fewer sleepless nights.
<<endif>>
===

title: Companion_Reminder_Pet
tags: companion ambient contextual
---
// Triggers when pet is idle (not defending or gathering)
<<if $petMode == "idle">>
{$companionName}: {$petName} is just sitting around. You could set them to Defend or Gather at the Pet House. Every Echo should earn their keep.
<<endif>>
===

title: Companion_FirstNight
tags: companion ambient atmosphere
---
// Triggers on first nightfall
{$companionName}: Night's falling. See those torches? The villagers light them every dusk.

{$companionName}: Enemies hit harder at night. Stay near the walls. And keep {$petName} close.

{$companionName}: If it gets too dark to see... well, that's why we need the Heartwood. Its glow keeps the worst things at bay.
===

title: Companion_FirstKill
tags: companion combat milestone
---
// Triggers on player's first enemy kill
{$companionName}: First blood. You felt that? The Heartwood just pulsed.

{$companionName}: Every enemy you stop, every wave you survive — the root grows a little stronger. And so do you.
===

title: Companion_FirstExplore
tags: companion exploration milestone
---
// Triggers when player first exits through a gate
{$companionName}: Beyond the walls. Welcome to the Marches.

{$companionName}: Stay alert. The Goblins don't announce themselves like the Orcs do. You'll know they're there when an arrow comes out of nowhere.

{$companionName}: Look for resource nodes — glowing spots on the ground. That's what we need. Claim them, and {$petName} can harvest while we push deeper.

{$companionName}: And remember — the Return Portal at any outpost gets you home instantly. Don't be too proud to run.
===

title: Companion_FirstDungeon
tags: companion exploration milestone
---
// Triggers when player finds a dungeon entrance
{$companionName}: Hold on. You see that?

{$companionName}: That's a sealed entrance. The Verdant Watch monks locked these down centuries ago.

{$companionName}: The seal's cracked. Whatever's inside has been waiting a long time.

-> Should we go in?
    {$companionName}: Your call. Dungeons are dangerous — traps, enemies, no easy escape.
    {$companionName}: But the rewards? Ancient weapons. Rare crafting materials. Lore that might tell us how to strengthen the Heartwood.
    {$companionName}: I'll go with you if you go.
-> Not yet.
    {$companionName}: Smart. Mark it on your map and come back when you're stronger. It's not going anywhere.
===
